Patch summary:
A QSRI fence whose wait gave up is not reset and reused while the GPU may
still signal it. After the 3 s wait for a vkQueueSignalReleaseImageANDROID
submission timed out (or its device was lost), the fence went back to the
pool, and the next submission reset it: invalid usage on a fence still in
use, seen as stalls on slow GPUs and under WSL2. Such a fence now waits in
an in-flight list and rejoins the pool once it has signaled; the pool
destroys it at the end if its work is over, and the reset of a pooled fence
tolerates a lost device.
DSA (desktop-subsystem-for-android) fixes the same reuse in its patch 0018.
diff --git a/host/vulkan/vk_android_native_buffer_operations.cpp b/host/vulkan/vk_android_native_buffer_operations.cpp
